meta {
  name: Get Prefferred Answer Endpoint
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: https://webexapis.com/v1/telephony/config/people/{{personid}}/preferredAnswerEndpoint
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  accept: application/json
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Query a specific user to find their devices that are available for control — the "Get Preferred
  Answer Endpoint" endpoint.

  **Parameters**
  - `personId` (path) — the user whose controllable devices/endpoints you want to list. Bound to
    `{{personid}}`.

  **Usage**: Returns each endpoint (softphone app, desk phone, etc.) registered to that user, along
  with its `id` — this is one of two ways to find a `callingDeviceId`/`endpointId` for the personal
  Call Controls requests (List Devices being the other).

  See https://github.com/TeamCCEP/DeskphoneControl for more info and a little web app that will
  help visualise these APIs.

  Reference: https://developer.webex.com/calling/docs/api/v1/user-call-settings-2-2/get-preferred-answer-endpoint

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}
